  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 8.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both parties should see how this was decided. The SGD 8.00 cancellation fee does not stand. POL-NS-01 is the only clause that can make a no-show fee chargeable, and it requires all four of its conditions to hold together. Not one of them does on this record. (a) The trip record carries no driver 'arrived' event at all: arrived_at is null. (b) The driver's own GPS trace, 49 fixes from 14:00:40 to 14:08:40, never comes closer than 5,661 m to the pickup pin at Changi Terminal 1, reaches 11,906 m at its furthest, and moves at roughly 46 km/h throughout; no fix falls inside the 150 m airport arrival radius, and qualifying_fix_count is 0. (c) The longest qualifying in-geofence run is 0 seconds against the 480-second minimum dwell fixed for an AIRPORT pickup, a 480-second shortfall. (d) The trip was terminated by the rider, not the driver, on the code RIDER_CHANGED_MIND, which is not one of the three codes limb (d) recognises. Because limb (b) fails with no qualifying in-radius fix anywhere in the 15 minutes before cancellation (13:53:40 to 14:08:40, which fully contains the trace), POL-NS-02 entitles the rider to a full refund of the fee, and POL-NS-06 independently refunds it in full for the waiting-period shortfall, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she answered messages. Nothing displaces that. POL-NS-03 needs the driver stationary within 400 m of the pin and he was 5,661 m away at his closest approach, so it does not apply. POL-NS-05 is engaged only where a trip_record 'arrived' event is shown to be false; there is no arrival marker on this record at all, so the clause never runs and no false-arrival record is entered against the driver in referrals. On the rider's own position: her trace shows 41 qualifying fixes, every one 13 to 23 m from the pin and stationary, far inside the 200 m rider-presence radius for an airport pickup, so nothing here rests on any failure by her. POL-NS-04 does not apply either, because 'no. cancelling.' is not a locating or coordinating message, but that makes no difference, since the refund follows from the driver's trace alone. On the driver's case: his explanation that the original fare did not cover airport queue time on a holiday and that he told the rider the price before pickup so she could decide is heard, but the loaded policy does not make a mid-trip fare re-quote a ground for or against the fee, and the re-quote is not what decides this case either way. The counterparty statement carries no weight_multiplier, so it enters neither the minimum nor the maximum of the confidence cap; it is consistent with the chat log, which records the driver's message 'fare is 120 now, cash, or you cancel' at 14:03:40 and the rider's 'no. cancelling.' at 14:07:40. No driver compensation is payable: POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not satisfied on any limb. The anti-farming check would not have blocked payment in any event, since driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1 against the threshold of 4 and 1 over 110 completed trips is 0.009 against the 0.08 rate, and POL-NS-09(c) and (d) do not fire. On confidence: the trip record, GPS trace, chat log and fare breakdown all read COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, and the facts that decide this case, namely no arrived event in the trip record and no in-radius fix in the trace, are carried at full weight by the trip record and the trace, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and the ruling rests on unimpaired evidence. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00609-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, but nothing in this ruling rests on it: the POL-NS-06(i) summing route is unavailable and unnecessary because there are no in-geofence intervals to sum. A rider-side claim about that missing advisory was discarded for not naming its issue code; it is recorded in the audit below and was not needed to reach the result. The fare arithmetic is sound in any event: SGD 8.00 is the greater of the AIRPORT zone-class fee of SGD 6.00 and the RYDE_XL vehicle-tier fee of SGD 8.00, exactly as the fare breakdown itemises, so there is no integrity defect under POL-NS-08(d). The SGD 8.00 was charged with refund_issued_sgd 0.0; it now goes back to the rider in full."
  },
