    "explanation": "Rider and driver: the SGD 8.00 cancellation fee is refunded in full. POL-NS-01 charges a no-show fee only if all four of its conditions hold, and every one of them fails on this record. Limb (a): the trip record must contain a driver 'arrived' event; EV-TRIP-00609 has arrived_at null and carries no such event, so the anchor clause fails at the outset. Limb (b): the trace must place the driver inside the 150 m airport arrival radius; EV-GPS-00609 puts his closest fix 5,661 m from the pin (furthest 11,906 m), with zero qualifying in-radius fixes, while his distinct speeds run 45.9-48.7 km/h, i.e. he was driving, not holding a pickup bay. POL-NS-02 is explicit that where the trace contains no qualifying in-radius fix at any point in the 15 minutes preceding cancellation (13:53:40-14:08:40, which fully contains this trace), the driver never arrived and the rider is entitled to a full refund. Limb (c): the minimum continuous in-geofence dwell for an AIRPORT pickup is 480 seconds; the longest qualifying run is 0 seconds, a 480-second shortfall on the trace's own shortfall_basis, and POL-NS-06 refunds the fee in full on that arithmetic whether or not the rider was present or responsive. Limb (d): the clause requires termination by the driver with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT; the record shows cancelled_by RIDER and code RIDER_CHANGED_MIND, which the clause does not recognise. Driving the points the two sides made: I accept the driver's submission that the rider elected to cancel and that no 'arrived' marker — false or otherwise — was ever tapped, so POL-NS-05 and its false-arrival referral are not engaged; I accept that the fee arithmetic is sound, the fee schedule producing the greater of the AIRPORT zone-class fee (SGD 6.00) and the RYDE_XL vehicle-tier fee (SGD 8.00), i.e. SGD 8.00, exactly the fare_breakdown line, so no POL-NS-08(d) defect exists; and I accept that the anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 1, below 4; 1/110 = 0.009, below 0.08). On the rider's side I accept the arrival, proximity, dwell and reason-code points above, her stationary presence at the pin (41 qualifying fixes, 13-23 m, 0 km/h, well inside the 200 m airport radius), and the chat record in which the driver wrote 'fare is 120 now, cash, or you cancel' at 14:03:40 and she replied 'no. cancelling.' at 14:07:40. That message is not itself the ground of decision — chargeability is fixed by POL-NS-01 alone — but the record is consistent with a rider cancellation prompted by it rather than any no-show. Driver compensation is null: POL-NS-07 requires POL-NS-01 satisfied in full, and POL-NS-03 pin-ambiguity goodwill is unavailable because the driver was never stationary within 400 m of the pin. On confidence: the deciding facts are carried by the trip record and the GPS trace, both COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the cap is 1.0. The MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00609-01 (weight 0.0) carries no deciding fact — with no in-geofence interval there is nothing for POL-NS-06(i) to sum — and the rider's claim resting on it without disclosing its MISSING_ARTIFACT issue is discarded, as the referee found. No POL-NS-08 limb fires (no clock skew, no sampling gap over 120 s, no chat truncation gap, and the fare line reconciles), so no POL-NS-09(e) escalation arises; the rider's profile fields played no part in this outcome."
