    "explanation": "To both parties. The SGD 8.00 cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-00609 cannot stand and is refunded in full to the rider.\n\nWhy the fee fails. POL-NS-01 permits a no-show cancellation fee only where all four conditions hold, and on this record none of them does. (a) The trip record contains no driver 'arrived' event — trip_record.arrived_at is null. (b) The driver's own GPS trace never enters the 150 m arrival radius for an AIRPORT pickup: his closest fix is 5,661 m from the pin and his furthest 11,906 m, and derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count is 0 across all 49 fixes from 14:00:40 to 14:08:40 (the 15 minutes before the 14:08:40 cancellation is fully covered, so there is no gap to hide in). (c) There is no dwell at all — the longest qualifying in-geofence run is 0 seconds against the 480-second minimum fixed for an AIRPORT pickup for the zone class, a 480-second shortfall. (d) The trip was ended by the rider, not the driver, and on cancellation_reason_code RIDER_CHANGED_MIND, which limb (d) does not recognise. With limb (b) failed and no qualifying in-radius fix anywhere in the window, POL-NS-02 entitles the rider to a full refund of the fee; POL-NS-06 independently refunds in full for the waiting-period shortfall, whether or not the rider was present or replied. POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) does not apply: the driver was moving at roughly 46 km/h and was never stationary and never within 400 m of the pin, so no pin-ambiguity goodwill arises.\n\nOn the driver's points. His concession that limbs (b) and (c) are not met is accepted and is decisive. His fare-integrity point is correct and accepted — the SGD 8.00 line equals the greater of the AIRPORT zone-class fee (SGD 6.00) and the RYDE_XL vehicle-tier fee (SGD 8.00), so POL-NS-08(d) raises no defect against him. His anti-farming point is also correct: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1 (below 4) and 1/110 = 0.009 (below 0.08), so no withholding trigger fires. Neither point rescues the fee, because POL-NS-07 compensation requires POL-NS-01 to be satisfied in full, which it is not; no compensation is payable to the driver. The driver's '120, cash, or cancel' chat message is not itself a ground under the loaded policy for reversing the fee, and I do not reverse it on that basis — the fee fails on POL-NS-01's own limbs. POL-NS-04 (rider contact unanswered) is correctly shown not to apply, because the rider's only message, 'no. cancelling.', is not a locating or coordinating message; but the refund does not depend on that clause, and her presence at the pin (41 fixes, roughly 13 to 23 m out, stationary) is uncontradicted.\n\nImpairment. EV-ADVIS-00609-01 (TRAFFIC_ADVISORY) is MISSING at weight_multiplier 0.0 with issue MISSING_ARTIFACT. Its absence is citable and it carries no deciding fact; it only makes POL-NS-06(i) accumulation unavailable, which changes nothing here as there are no in-geofence intervals to sum. The four carriers of the deciding facts (trip record, GPS trace, chat log, fare breakdown) are all COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0 with no issue codes, so no confidence cap applies and the finding survives at full weight.\n\nNo referral and no escalation. POL-NS-05(ii) is not engaged because the driver never tapped a false 'arrived' marker to be caught, so no false-arrival referral arises. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: no artifact contradiction, no repeat-party dispute pattern (both disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0), no anti-farming trip and no_show_disputes_30d of 0, and no deciding artifact impaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (d). The contested SGD 8.00 is returned to the rider and the charge is released.",
